module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Segre.Mono
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Segre.Morphism

/-!
# The residue of [Stacks, Tag 01WD] is two statements about the Segre chart and its ring

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Segre/Morphism.lean` reduces Tag 01WD — and with it Chow's
lemma over a Noetherian base — to
`CategoryTheory.Mono (AlgebraicGeometry.Segre.segreMorphism n m)`. This file reduces *that* to
exactly two hypotheses, by instantiating the chart criterion
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceSections.mono_morphismAtUniverse` at the Segre data:

1. every Segre chart is **affine**, and
2. the Segre chart ring homomorphism `ℤ[Z₀, …, Z_N] ⟶ Γ(chart, 𝒪)` is **surjective** — i.e. the
   ratios `Z_{ab} / Z_{ij}` generate the chart's ring.

Both are statements about one open subscheme of `ℙⁿ_ℤ ×_{Spec ℤ} ℙᵐ_ℤ` and its ring of functions;
neither mentions a morphism, a monomorphism, or projective space of dimension `nm+n+m`.

## What is still missing, and it is four named bricks

The two hypotheses are not proved here. Both are about the chart
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceSections.nonvanishingChart (segreModule n m) (segreSections n m k)`, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Segre.nonvanishingOpen_segreSection` identifies with
`pr₁⁻¹(ℙⁿ)_{Xᵢ} ⊓ pr₂⁻¹(ℙᵐ)_{Yⱼ}`, the two factors being nonvanishing loci of the coordinate
sections of `𝒪(1)`. What is owed:

* the nonvanishing locus of the coordinate section is only known to **contain** `D₊(Xᵢ)`
  (`Stacks.ProjTwistSection.basicOpen_le_nonvanishingOpen_homogeneousSection` is an inequality);
  without the equality the chart is not identified with a product of standard opens at all;
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.divBySection_tensorSections` turns the chart ratios into products of a
  ratio on `ℙⁿ` and a ratio on `ℙᵐ`, but the **pullback** half — the ratio of two pulled-back
  sections is the pullback of the ratio — is not stated anywhere;
* affineness of `D₊(Xᵢ) ×_{Spec ℤ} D₊(Yⱼ)` as an open of the fibre product, and the
  identification of its ring with `Aᵢ ⊗_ℤ Bⱼ` under `pr₁^*` and `pr₂^*`;
* the assembly. Note that the last algebraic step is **already available**:
  `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.chartHom_surjective` says `Away (ℤ[X], Xᵢ)` is generated by the ratios
  `X_a / Xᵢ`, which is the generation statement each factor contributes.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Segre.mono_segreMorphism_of_chart`: **`Mono (segreMorphism n m)` from the two
  chart hypotheses.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Segre.hasSegreMonoZ_of_chart`: the same two hypotheses give
  `AlgebraicGeometry.HasSegreMonoZ`, and hence — by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.hasDenseChowModification_of_hasSegreMonoZ` — Chow's lemma over a Noetherian
  base, dense-open clause included.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks 01WD]` attribute is attached: every statement here is conditional.

The instantiation needed no transport: `AlgebraicGeometry.Segre.segreMorphism` is by definition
`morphismAtUniverse` of the Segre data, so the criterion applies by a bare term application, and
none of the four `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`-is-a-`def` cure families was needed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0200](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0200)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NF)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceSections

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Segre

/-- **`Mono (segreMorphism n m)` from two statements about the Segre chart**: that it is affine,
and that its ring is generated by the ratios `Z_{ab} / Z_{ij}`. This is
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceSections.mono_morphismAtUniverse` at the Segre data, the covering
hypothesis being
`AlgebraicGeometry.Segre.iSup_nonvanishingChart_segreSections_eq_top`. -/
theorem mono_segreMorphism_of_chart (n m : ℕ)
    (haff : ∀ k, IsAffine
      (nonvanishingChart (segreModule.{u} n m) (segreSections.{u} n m k)).toScheme)
    (hsurj : ∀ k, Function.Surjective
      (chartHom (segreModule.{u} n m) (segreSections.{u} n m) k)) :
    Mono (segreMorphism.{u} n m) :=
  mono_morphismAtUniverse (segreModule.{u} n m) (segreSections.{u} n m)
    (iSup_nonvanishingChart_segreSections_eq_top.{u} n m) haff hsurj

/-- **The two chart statements give `AlgebraicGeometry.HasSegreMonoZ`**, which is the single
hypothesis of `AlgebraicGeometry.hasDenseChowModification_of_hasSegreMonoZ`: so Chow's
lemma over a Noetherian base — dense-open clause included — rests on exactly these two. -/
theorem hasSegreMonoZ_of_chart
    (haff : ∀ (n m : ℕ) k, IsAffine
      (nonvanishingChart (segreModule.{u} n m) (segreSections.{u} n m k)).toScheme)
    (hsurj : ∀ (n m : ℕ) k, Function.Surjective
      (chartHom (segreModule.{u} n m) (segreSections.{u} n m) k)) :
    HasSegreMonoZ.{u} :=
  hasSegreMonoZ_of_mono.{u} fun n m =>
    mono_segreMorphism_of_chart.{u} n m (haff n m) (hsurj n m)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Segre

end
